{
  "presses": ["L-index-home-in", "L-middle-home", "R-index-home-in", "R-middle-home"],
  "note": "T1 done. After symbols list, next use same 4 positions but swap each key to its nearest neighbor (±row/±side) to start building key→letter map."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-index-top-in", "R-index-top-in", "L-middle-bottom", "L-ring-home"],
  "note": "T3 {L-index-top-in,L-middle-top,R-index-top-in,R-middle-top}={C,H,L,V}; rot3{L-middle-bottom,L-middle-top,L-ring-home} (so L-middle-top swaps among those 3)."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-middle-bottom", "R-middle-top", "L-index-top-in"],
  "locks": {"L-pinky-top": "A", "L-middle-bottom": "L"},
  "note": "Now: {L-pinky-top=A, L-middle-bottom=L, R-middle-top=V}. Chord adds Li-top-in to learn {C,H} for Li; then Ri-top-in=other."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-middle-bottom", "R-middle-top", "L-index-home-in"],
  "locks": {
    "L-pinky-top": "A",
    "L-middle-bottom": "L",
    "R-middle-top": "V",
    "L-index-top-in": "H"
  },
  "note": "Known: L-pinky-top=A, L-middle-bottom=L, R-middle-top=V, L-index-top-in=H. Next read L-index-home-in by chord with these 3."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-ring-home", "R-ring-home", "R-index-top-in"],
  "locks": {
    "L-pinky-top": "A",
    "L-ring-home": "O",
    "R-ring-home": "M"
  },
  "note": "Known A@L-pT,O@L-rH,M@R-rH,Y@L-iH-in,Z@R-pT,J@R-rT,V@R-mT. Next: press L-pT,L-rH,R-rH,R-iT-in; deduce R-iT-in if no rotation hits anchors."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "R-index-home-in", "R-index-top-in", "R-index-bottom-in"],
  "note": "LpT/LrH={A,O}. Known RiH-in=N, RiT-in=C. Next: use turn18 with LpT,RiH-in,RiT-in (swap 4th key) and intersect symbol-sets to get LpT."
}

{
  "presses": ["R-middle-top", "L-pinky-top", "L-ring-home", "R-index-top-in"],
  "note": "From {L-pT,L-rH,R-mT,R-mH}={A,O,F,V} and no rotations: {R-mT,R-mH}={F,V}. Next press R-mT with L-pT(A),L-rH(O),R-iT-in(C) => deduce R-mT; R-mH=other."
}
